#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:0
#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:8
msgid "raw-volume interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:10
msgid ""
"`raw-volume` provides access to a specific disk partition. This interface is "
"restricted because it provides privileged access to device partitions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:12
msgid ""
"The slot is intended to be implemented by a gadget snap and is not provided "
"by the core system snap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:14
msgid "**Auto-Connect**: no **Attributes**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:16
msgid "`path` (slot): path to device partition e.g. `/dev/mmcblk0p1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:19
msgid ""
"This interface controls a resource shared by the whole system. Snaps that "
"use it can be installed as parallel instances, but every instance acts on "
"the same system resource and snapd does not coordinate between them. Make "
"sure each instance manages different resources, or run only one instance at "
"a time. See {ref}`Snaps that are unsupported as parallel instances "
"<interfaces-parallel-installs-shared-resources>` for details.."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:22
msgid "Requires snapd version *2.43+*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:24
msgid ""
"To use a disk partition, the snap developer must add `plugs: [ raw-volume ]` "
"to a snap's [snapcraft.yaml](https://documentation.ubuntu.com/snapcraft/"
"stable/reference/project-file/snapcraft-yaml). The snap user can then access "
"a specific disk partition with an {ref}`interface connection <explanation-"
"interfaces-all-about-interfaces>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:26
msgid ""
"Use  `snap interface raw-volume` to see which disk partitions are available "
"on the system for snaps to use:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:28
msgid ""
"$ snap interface raw-volume\n"
"name:    raw-volume\n"
"summary: allows access to specific disk partition\n"
"slots:\n"
"  - foo:mmcblk0p1\n"
"  - foo:mmcblk0p2\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/raw-volume-interface.md:37
msgid ""
"Once connected, the consuming snap can use the device via the path specified "
"by the connected slot."
msgstr ""
